{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested: the 26 October sprint report. Head 8972657ec49af7f521312e24e72e87885603ea23, branch planner/sprint-report-20261026: one commit on Main a97c7425 (merge base equals Main), one new file, notes/reports/2026-10-26-sprint-report.md (191 lines). Review request 405353f4 (refiled; it replaces ee9545fd), checker promise 07d73d41, request f99104f0 (planner promise a56a296d). Artifacts: the report (343a7aa6) and the notes directory (350cf6c2).\n\nRead order: the report at the head in full; the review conditions; git log --first-parent for the window; each cited act; the day's survey asserts for the figures; then the two scripts.\n\nOne gap blocks approval:\n1. Landings. The report covers 17:00 on 25 October to 17:00 on 26 October and says six heads landed (lines 5-8; list at lines 91-104). git log --first-parent a97c7425 shows eight landings in that window. These two are missing:\n   - d1c3622f, 25 October 17:14: the 25 October sprint report (request d4d19eaa, approval 90814d78).\n   - 575c113f, 25 October 18:45: the advisory notes and evidence warnings in the gate, scripts/check-notes.mjs (request 28b878ed, approval db227d78).\n   Add both, or move the window's start to after 18:45 and say so. Request f99104f0 says \"the six landings\" too.\n\nSmall fixes worth making in the same recut (not blocking):\n2. Lines 77-79 and 141-142 state planner answer 92278157 more broadly than it is. The answer covers a head that \"deletes, moves or edits a file under docs, notes or apps/room/docs that another actor published\". Such a head \"names that directory in its own artifact filing\", meaning the area directory such as docs. The answer does not say \"parent directory\", \"first artifact filing\", or files anywhere in the repository.\n3. Line 77: \"the merge superseded the pointer\". Line 72 uses \"pointer\" for the pointer to the commit that holds the removed files, so this reads as if the merge removed that pointer. Name what the merge superseded: the planner's docs artifact 42e1aca1, whose successor is ff5f4f04 (landing check 03e852f7). 92278157 had said that artifact stays live; the merge retired it anyway.\n4. Lines 130-133 cite e17cbaa4 for \"the head creates register 20, directory 19, rules 12, destination 15\". e17cbaa4 keeps Rules 11, Destination 14, Register 19 and Directory 18 exact, reserves Destination 15, and allows a Register, Directory or Rules version only if their data or rules change. The four numbers come from the builder's plan in promise f82aba22 (14:40). Cite both, or say \"plans to create\". Line 134 (the declined answer that names the intervening entry, with no kernel change) is e17cbaa4 item 2; give the identifier there too.\n\nConditions met:\n- Identifiers. Every commit named resolves:\n  - 9daa037e landed 25 October 22:34; 6852f78d at 09:36 (61 commits and 85 paths, as stated); d36773b3 at 10:00; 986c7120 at 10:14; 197acc83 at 14:33; a97c7425 at 14:36.\n  - 52c2714c (02:24) and 8ba23a34 are R7 branch commits. The builder's acts stop at 02:41 and resume at 08:14.\n  - The acts say what the sentences say. 036e7f12: two chained repairs on four conditions, and a third failure needs one ordinary gate at the exact head. 21c4328b: approved at 09:32. 8d8eef89: the documentation follow-up. 5e6d482c: the hardening head. cf0328ba: the BR-9 gate and the R7 native run as before points. 29be9662: Lending runs in its own one-worker project between scope and scope-denial. 92278157: see item 2. 499b2a80: measure and cut. a455fdba and 30d4cf83: the research note and its review.\n- Figures. These match the planner's survey asserts:\n  - Worker versions (877fd3a4, e2ff4a5f): dap-grow 50243006 at 23:33, e47aac4d at 23:51 and 38facfa8 at 00:09, all from 9daa037e; abed606d, dap-demo 8962e21e and dap-lending 4b9afd11 at 14:38 from a97c7425.\n  - Room A at 9,824 (877fd3a4) and at 24,333 (499b2a80). Site restart generation 2 resumed at 1,797 and reached its frontier of 7,947 at 06:35 (b6d02a35).\n  - The 15:35 shortfalls: 2,504,897 + 1,734,272 - 4,194,304 = 44,865, and Site 2,606,063 + 1,588,518 - 4,194,304 = 277.\n  - \"About 900 entries an hour\": 14,509 entries in about 15.8 hours.\n  - BR-3: the failed gates took 887.092 s and 852.986 s, and G3 took 882.237 s with native 780 passed and 2 skipped (BR-3 note, lines 112, 118 and 127).\n- Work only. The report describes work, rulings and outcomes. The guidance at lines 178-180 is the planner's guidance to the builder (34c8885a).\n- Prose lines are at most 79 characters. There are no longer lines outside table rows, and git diff --check is clean.\n- At the head, check-notes a97c7425..8972657e reports 0 warnings, and check-doc-links reports 705 relative links checked and 0 broken (run on an exported tree of the head). The report has no Markdown links.\n\nArchitecture, Security and Simplification: not applicable beyond accuracy. The head is one prose report with no code, configuration, authority or deployment change.\n\nNote for the planner (not a gap in this head): request 499b2a80 says Room A \"archived about 9,000 entries today\" on 38facfa8 and about 650 more after 14:38. The survey figures are 9,824 at 00:11, 16,545 at 06:38 and 24,333 at 15:35, which is about 14,500. The report's figures are the correct ones.\n\nThe shared checkout is clean again (git status empty at 18:52), so this report and the research note can land after approval.\n\nVerdict: changes requested at exact head 8972657e. A recut that changes only this report needs no gate. I will review it at its exact head.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:343a7aa6893a5242a9260364c0fac88b37b43084","binding":"assigned","head":"8972657ec49af7f521312e24e72e87885603ea23","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:07d73d414396601cae8ef6e4b88e8448ed196aa2\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:a56a296d9d6359922d9a3f7e19a983894a4